      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T00:48:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t look too hard, so please tell me to look harder if this is a silly question. Should `delegate_accepted_image_metadata_` and `started_incremental_decode_` combine into a state enum?",
      "revId": "349a0b61e9fda4ce3e7a74411124e208fe37052e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c15fbc5d_9139d1c0",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 7232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T18:37:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure.  Let\u0027s talk? :-)\n\nThe states are:\n\n* No `decoder_` (i.e. have to call `decoder_ \u003d SkPngRustDecoder::Decode(...)`)\n* Got `decoder_`, but no successful `PngReadHeader` call yet - this is tracked via `delegate_accepted_image_metadata_` (and delegate provides `target_gamma_`)\n* Got `decoder_`, `delegate_accepted_image_metadata_`, but haven\u0027t successfully called `startIncrementalDecode` yet - this is tracked via `started_incremental_decode_`\n* Finished (i.e. `incrementalDecode` succeeded + we called delegate\u0027s `PngFinishedDecoding`) - not really tracked, except by resetting `decoder_`\n\nRetrying/continuing after `PngReadHeader` returns a failure is unnecessary.  Let me get rid of this part of tracking.\n\nAnd let me try introducing an explicit `enum`.  I wish I had Rust `enum`s where some states would have a `SkCodec` and others wouldn\u0027t.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "996d5204_e4d7dde0",
      "revId": "349a0b61e9fda4ce3e7a74411124e208fe37052e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbc0329d_fa2f8ca8",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T00:48:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be ok to not worry about this and avoid storing `codec_memory_`? Just always use `codec_memory`.",
      "revId": "349a0b61e9fda4ce3e7a74411124e208fe37052e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e40532ea_125838ed",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 105,
      "author": {
        "id": 7232
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T18:37:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We wrap `CFX_CodecMemory` in `CodecMemoryStream:SkStream` and give up ownership of the stream to `SkCodec` (in ` decoder_ \u003d SkPngRustDecoder::Decode(std::move(stream), ...);` call).  But `decoder_` is long-lived and so when we try to use `decoder_` in a new `ContinueDecoding(maybe_new_codec_memory)` call, the `decoder_`\u0027s stream will still refer to the original codec memory.\n\nAt one point I took care of this more explicitly (but I think it is not really needed).  In the past I:\n\n* Stored `SkiaPngContext*` in `CodecMemoryStream`\n* Stored `RetainPtr\u003cCFX_CodecMemory\u003e` in `CodecMemoryStream` but **only for the duration of** execution of `SkiaPngContext::ContinueDecode`\n* Had `CodecMemoryStream` reach out to `SkiaPngContext`\u0027s `CFX_CodecMemory` for reads\n\nBut I think the current patchset is okay + it is simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "bbc0329d_fa2f8ca8",
      "revId": "349a0b61e9fda4ce3e7a74411124e208fe37052e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0d1a804_ba96637b",
        "filename": "core/fxcodec/png/skia_png_decoder.cpp",
